    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on capitalizing on several favorable matchups against right-handed pitching, specifically against Zac Gallen. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is our clear headliner today with a 71.78 score; despite facing a lefty in Framber Valdez, his elite plate discipline and the fact that Valdez allows for high-efficiency stolen base opportunities against his slower delivery make him a must-start. Joining him at the top of the production hierarchy are **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) and **Luis Arraez** (64.18). Both benefit significantly from the +8% SP skill adjustment and a favorable platoon advantage against Gallen, with **Jung Hoo Lee** further boosted by a prime lead-off spot that maximizes his run-scoring potential. **Geraldo Perdomo** also earns a strong recommendation (64.00) despite a tougher matchup against Ray, as his promotion to the #3 spot provides a necessary floor in our 5x5 build.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jeremiah Jackson** on the bench. He hovered near the 40-point threshold with a score of 39.75, but the combination of a bottom-third order placement and the difficulty of facing McClanahan ultimately forced our hand to prioritize the higher-ceiling utility of **Gavin Sheets** and the park factors favoring **Tyler Freeman**. Speaking of **Tyler Freeman**, he remains our biggest risk factor today; while his 60.91 score is promising, it is contingent on a pending lineup confirmation. Should he drop out of the #3 spot, his value\u2014and our overall team efficiency\u2014will fluctuate. \n\nWe are also monitoring the heavy platoon weightings impacting **Bryson Stott** (48.83) and **Daulton Varsho** (48.46). While both are technically \"Marginal\" starts today due to the L/L matchups, the inclusion of **Daulton Varsho** is bolstered by the 100% stolen base efficiency signal against a slow-delivering pitcher, which is crucial given our heavy weighting of speed. Meanwhile, we continue to hold **Cal Raleigh** and **Dylan Beavers** on the shelf due to injury, keeping our active rotation focused on high-contact players like **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman** to stabilize our AVG and RBI categories while we navigate the high-leverage spots on the schedule.",
